#=GF RT   Evidence for a second class of S-adenosylmethionine riboswitches and other
#=GF RT   regulatory RNA motifs in alpha-proteobacteria.
#=GF RA   Corbino KA, Barrick JE, Lim J, Welz R, Tucker BJ, Puskarz I, Mandal M,
#=GF RA   Rudnick ND, Breaker RR
#=GF RL   Genome Biol. 2005;6:R70.
#=GF CC   This family is a riboswitch found predominantly in alpha-proteobacteria
#=GF CC   that binds S-adenosyl methionine (SAM). Its structure and sequence appear
#=GF CC   to be unrelated to the SAM riboswitch Rfam:RF00162 found in Gram-positive
#=GF CC   bacteria. This SAM riboswitch is located upstream of the metA and metC
#=GF CC   genes in Agrobacterium tumefaciens, and other methionine and SAM
#=GF CC   biosynthesis genes in other alpha-proteobacteria. Like the other SAM
#=GF CC   riboswitch, it probably functions to turn off expression of these genes in
#=GF CC   response to elevated SAM levels.
#=GF WK   SAM-II_riboswitch
#=GF SQ   40

